<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pollentia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pollentia was a Roman town on the north-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Mallorca</a>, next to modern Alcúdia, founded by Quintus Caecilius Metellus after his conquest of the Balearics in 123 BCE. It became the island's most important Roman city, with a forum, temples and a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, before declining in late antiquity after attacks in the 5th century. Its excavated remains are the largest Roman site in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pollentia.jpg" alt="Pollentia" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Docchi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pollenzo_San_Vittore.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
